      "kind": "see",
      "title": "See it",
      "text": "The wazir moves one square up, down, left or right, and takes the same way. It is one of the oldest fairy pieces: old large forms of chess, such as Tamerlane chess, had it, and many newer pieces are built from it. The marked squares are every square it can reach.",
