      "square": "d4"
    },
    {
      "kind": "try",
      "title": "Try it",
      "text": "Move the wazir to the marked square. It takes two moves.",
      "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "w": "wazir" }, "fen": "7k/8/8/8/3W4/8/8/K7 w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } },
      "square": "d4",
      "targets": ["e5"]
    },
    {
      "kind": "read",
      "title": "Strategy",
      "pages": [
        {
          "text": "The wazir is a weak piece, worth a little more than a pawn. It is slow, so bring it close to the action early. Unlike the fers, it changes square colour with every move, so in time it can reach any square.",
          "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "w": "wazir" }, "fen": "4k3/8/8/8/3W4/8/8/4K3 w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } },
          "arrows": [["d4", "d5"]]
        },
        {
          "text": "A wazir protects the pieces next to it up, down, left and right. Two wazirs side by side guard each other, so neither can be taken for free, and they can walk up the board together.",
          "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "w": "wazir" }, "fen": "4k3/8/8/8/3WW3/8/8/4K3 w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } },
          "arrows": [["d4", "d5"]]
        },
        {
          "text": "A wazir can't attack diagonally. Here the black fers attacks the wazir from e5, and the wazir can't take it back, so it must step away.",
          "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "w": "wazir", "f": "fers" }, "fen": "4k3/8/8/4f3/3W4/8/8/4K3 w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } },
          "arrows": [["d4", "d3"]]
        }
      ]
    },
